The **`tokenizerId`** property.

In that test (packages/core/test/cache.test.ts, the one titled *"records the injected tokenizer id on every outcome so swapping tokenizers is a deliberate diff rather than a silent shift of every recorded range (§17)"*), the assertions are:

```ts
const heuristic = new ProviderCacheSimulator({ tokenizer: h.tokenizer }).submit(prompt);
const bytes = new ProviderCacheSimulator({
  tokenizer: new ExactTokenizer('bytes-v0', (text) => text.length),
}).submit(prompt);

expect(bytes.tokenizerId).toBe('bytes-v0');          // ← the property
expect(bytes.total).not.toBe(heuristic.total);
expect(bytes.segments.map((s) => s.blockIds)).toEqual(heuristic.segments.map((s) => s.blockIds));
```

So while the segment *structure* (`blockIds` per segment) must match the heuristic tokenizer's, and the *totals* must differ, the `bytes` outcome's `tokenizerId` is the property pinned to `'bytes-v0'` — stamping the injected tokenizer id on every outcome so a tokenizer swap shows up as an explicit diff in recorded ranges rather than silently shifting them.

